    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, can you help me write a brief for a stakeholder? Need to explain the difference between vertical and horizontal scaling in AWS. I want to keep it simple so they get why we need Auto Scaling groups for traffic spikes, but keep it professional. Thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Vertical scaling involves upgrading an existing server's resources, such as memory or CPU, to handle increased load. In contrast, horizontal scaling adds more servers to distribute traffic, which is generally more stable and cost-effective for large loads. For your explanation, Auto Scaling groups are essential because they automatically add new horizontal instances during traffic spikes, ensuring service reliability without manual intervention. This approach optimizes costs by only maintaining the necessary resources while preventing service degradation during peak times.",
      "source": "target",
